title: 'pallet-revive: add `burn` to the `System` pre-compile'
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The `System` pre-compile at `0x900` gains `burn(uint256 amount)`. It removes `amount` of the
    native token from the balance of its caller and from the total issuance. The caller is the
    contract or account that calls the pre-compile, so a contract burns its own funds and an
    account that calls the pre-compile directly burns its own. `amount` is in the unit of
    `msg.value`. The existential deposit stays. Burning dust the caller does not hold converts
    one unit of balance into dust first, so that unit has to be spendable as well.

    The call reverts when the spendable balance of the caller, without the existential deposit
    and without held or frozen funds, is lower than `amount`, when `amount` does not fit the
    balance type of the chain, when value is sent along, or when the pre-compile is reached
    through a delegate call. In a static context it fails without revert data. A call started by
    root fails with `RootNotAllowed`. A burn is undone together with the frame it happened in
    when that frame reverts.

    The whole units burned are reported as `Balances::Burned`. A burn of dust only emits no
    event, and a burn that first converts one unit into dust emits a `Burned` of one unit before
    the one of the amount, so the sum of `Burned` amounts can exceed the amount requested. No
    EVM log is emitted.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Contracts can now reduce the total issuance. `System.burn` does not use `Config::OnBurn`,
    and a runtime cannot opt out of it. A runtime that redirects burned value to a treasury
    through `OnBurn` keeps doing so for the gas rounding only. No migration is needed.

    `pallet_revive::WeightInfo` gains the required method `burn(d: u32)`, where `d` is 1 when
    `amount` has a dust part. Runtimes using `SubstrateWeight` or `()` need no change. Runtimes
    with their own `WeightInfo` implementation stop compiling until they implement the method,
    and should regenerate their weights with the new `burn` benchmark.

    The `ISystemCalls` enum of `pallet-revive-uapi` gains a `burn` variant. Code that matches on
    it exhaustively has to add an arm.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-uapi
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
